      "writtenOn": "2018-02-23T18:57:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After max17055 is configured to measure temperature by NTC thermistor in the battery pack, I see max17055 still needs ~1 sec to find battery is absent. So the answer is yes if battery_is_present() is not called within the 1 sec window. \n\nUnfortunately I do see battery_is_present() be called a few time within this window during boot and report \u0027battery is present\u0027 even though battery is absent... \nFortunately I don\u0027t see catastrophic effect from those wrong reports of battery status.\n\nWe can add a delay in max17055_init() to wait until battery_is_present() reliable, but IMO it\u0027s not worth the increase of the boot time since \u0027booting w/o battery\u0027 is really a rare use case.",
